repository-code: "https://github.com/nabolitains/SAM-NeuroAdapt"
abstract: >-
  A brain-extraction pipeline that uses no task-specific model training: a template is
  selected from a 21-atlas lifespan library (by recorded age when available), registered to
  the subject, and used to prompt a frozen Segment Anything Model 2; the mask is then refined
  by classical intensity-based methods. A stage-wise ablation shows that the matched atlas,
  rather than the foundation model, drives overlap accuracy and contains failures.
keywords:
  - skull-stripping
  - brain extraction
  - Segment Anything Model
  - zero-shot segmentation
  - multi-atlas registration
  - reproducibility
  - neuroimaging
